ke its start low); investor cycle overdue). This is an UNCONFIRMED TURN, not a confirmed buy. Weekly confirmation lags price, so this exact reading covers BOTH bounces that fail AND the first leg of a genuine new cycle \u2014 you can't tell which in real time, so treat it as a risk/size signal, not a direction call. Measured: weekly-unconfirmed bottoming setups held the low ~49% of the time vs ~68% once the weekly turns up. The daily cycle has also failed (broke its own start low), which tilts the odds toward failure here.", "next": "Nimble traders only \u2014 small size, defined stop below 8.96. Not an investment buy yet. What would upgrade it: weekly momentum turning up, a reclaim of the investor-cycle low, or the first daily cycle right-translating \u2014 add on confirmation, not ahead of it.", "weekly_ok": false, "regime": "bear", "regime_label": "BEARISH", "regime_why": "weekly momentum negative; investor cycle failed (broke its start low); investor cycle overdue", "regime_score": -5.0, "regime_line": "Bigger picture: BEARISH \u2014 weekly momentum negative; investor cycle failed (broke its start low); investor cycle overdue (investor cycle week 27 \u00b7 failed \u00b7 daily cycle broke its start low 33d ago).", "summary_line": "Short-term (daily): unconfirmed turn. Bigger picture (counter-trend): bearish.", "points": ["Bigger picture is bearish (counter-trend for a daily long)", "Macro: US net liquidity neutral \u2014 no macro tilt on the odds", "\u26a0 Failed cycle \u2014 price broke below the low that began this cycle (33d ago)", "Swing low printed (buyers rejected the low)", "Back above the 10-day average", "Daily momentum ~3 bars from turning up"], "entry": {"tag": "UNCONFIRMED \u2014 HIGH RISK", "tag_zh": "\u672a\u786e\u8ba4 \u2014 \u9ad8\u98ce\u9669", "urgency": "caution", "text": "An unconfirmed turn: a daily low is forming while the bigger picture is still bearish. Nimble traders only \u2014 small size, defined stop below 8.96. Not an investment buy un